The paper-local standard-library verifier enumerates every source and target
in 26 boxes, including $n=1$ through length ten, $n=2$ through length seven,
and $n=3,4,5$ at shorter lengths.  It compares literal iterates with
Theorem~\ref{thm:iterate}, reconstructs every target by a cyclic path dynamic
program, attacks matrix direction by dense products, and checks integer
eigenspace bases.  Selected results appear in Table~\ref{tab:control}.

